{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_b6317c214d9f36fe","type":"tool_result","content":"## summary : Gap is a ROCm device-mask leak, not a model gap: Qwen3_5ForConditionalGeneration IS registered and runnable in the live serving env (/opt/envs/wu1w). A/B on the real Magpie path under the inherited leak (ROCR=0 vs HIP=2): control -> EngineCore 'No CUDA GPUs are available'; with only the proposed extra_envs HIP/CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 (logical index) -> SUCCESS, /health 200, result.json. No new patch: the kept reconciliation patch applies cleanly; the client install is verified live.\n## confidence : 0.9\n## empty : False\n## gap_canonical_id : gap.enablement.unknown\n## domain : enablement_specialist\n## patches_written: []\n## artifacts: []\n## setup_commands: []\n## new_findings:\n - {\"accuracy_risk\": \"none\", \"domain_tags\": [\"vllm\", \"qwen3_5\", \"gdn\", \"hybrid_attention\", \"runnability\", \"enablement\", \"gfx90a\"], \"expected_impact\": \"Reframes the round entirely: no ladder climb (Rung 2-5) is needed for this model, so a config-only delta is the correct and sufficient deliverable.\", \"source\": \"/mnt/stripe-3mix-3t2/models/davetha/Qwen3.8-27B-ABLITERATED-W8A8-gdnint8/config.json; /opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/model_executor/models/registry.py:203-204,592-595; in-session logs/repro_server.log + logs/reproB_fixed.log (port 8899, GPU 0, exact production server_args from manifest.json)\", \"what\": \"The gap 'vllm cannot launch Qwen3.8-27B-ABLITERATED-W8A8-gdnint8: unknown' is NOT an architecture/weight/kernel enablement gap. architectures=['Qwen3_5ForConditionalGeneration'] / model_type=qwen3_5 IS in the LIVE serving env's registry (registry.py:592 -> qwen3_5.Qwen\n - {\"accuracy_risk\": \"none\", \"domain_tags\": [\"rocm\", \"device-visibility\", \"enablement\", \"magpie\", \"inferencex\"], \"expected_impact\": \"This is the single blocker to booting at all; pinning HIP/CUDA to the logical index clears it (measured, not inferred).\", \"source\": \"in-session scratch/e2e_control/variant_00_specialist-rebench/benchmark_vllm_20260914_153851/server.log (gpu_worker.py:379 -> torch/cuda/__init__.py:501) vs scratch/e2e_fixed/variant_00_specialist-rebench/benchmark_vllm_20260914_153258/inferencex_result.json + logs/e2e_fixed.json; /opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/platforms/rocm.py:127-156\", \"what\": \"PROVEN BY A/B ON THE PRODUCTION GATE PATH with the kept Magpie patch NOT live (it applies cleanly but is currently reverted in the tree): the harness inherits ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 + HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=2. Counts are equal, so torch._parse_visible_devices() passes and \n - {\"accuracy_risk\": \"none\", \"domain_tags\": [\"hyperloom\", \"magpie\", \"grid_semantics\", \"enablement\"], \"expected_impact\": \"Prevents a future round from proposing unset_envs or 'just unset HIP', which look correct but are provably inert against an inherited var.\", \"source\": \"/opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/Magpie/modes/benchmark/benchmarker.py:776,800; /opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/hyperloom/orchestrator/actions/executors/_grid_runner.py:664-671; InferenceX@3d55815/benchmarks/vllm_mi300x.sh:63-68\", \"what\": \"Only one config mechanism can fix the leak, and the obvious alternative cannot. A variant's extra_envs is written into benchmark.envs, which Magpie applies OVER an os.environ.copy() in _build_local_command (benchmarker.py:776 'env = os.environ.copy()', then :800 'for key, value in env_vars.items(): env[key] = str(value)') -> it DOES override an inherited leak. unse\n - {\"accuracy_risk\": \"none\", \"domain_tags\": [\"vllm\", \"rocm\", \"device-visibility\", \"enablement\"], \"expected_impact\": \"Makes the enablement delta robust to whichever mask the harness leaks, instead of trading one failure mode for another.\", \"source\": \"/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/platforms/rocm.py:127-156; in-session scratch/e2e_fixed/variant_00_specialist-rebench/config.yaml (ROCR=0, HIP=0, CUDA=0) + its server.log\", \"what\": \"HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES and CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES must be set TOGETHER and EQUAL, so the delta is atomic. vLLM's _sync_hip_cuda_env_vars() runs at import, raises a hard ValueError on any HIP/CUDA disagreement, and copies an inherited CUDA value onto HIP when HIP is unset. A one-sided pin (HIP=0 while CUDA leaks a physical id) converts a device-selection bug into an import-time crash. Validated empirically: the successful boot had ROCR=0 + HIP=0 + CUDA=0 a\n - {\"accuracy_risk\": \"none\", \"domain_tags\": [\"environment\", \"magpie\", \"inferencex\", \"lifecycle\", \"enablement\"], \"expected_impact\": \"Removes two phantom gaps so the next round spends its budget on the real gate (accuracy/throughput) instead of re-diagnosing the launcher.\", \"source\": \"in-session /opt/venv/bin/python3 -c 'import huggingface_hub, transformers'; InferenceX@3d55815/benchmarks/benchmark_lib.sh:682,870-885; runs/baseline/48e0ae2b0af74c03b4b40c847fc99d3b/benchmark_vllm_20260914_151400/server.log; ps/ss/rocm-smi probes\", \"what\": \"Both blockers the prior round named as its 'next domino' are ALREADY resolved, so neither needs re-authoring. (1) bench-client deps: /opt/venv/bin/python3 (first on the gate's PATH, and the bare 'python3' benchmark_lib.sh:682 uses) now imports huggingface_hub 1.29.0 + transformers 5.16.1, i.e. the recorded setup_commands were replayed and the ModuleNotFoundE\n - {\"accuracy_risk\": \"none\", \"domain_tags\": [\"integration\", \"allowlist\", \"venv-routing\", \"enablement\", \"aiter\", \"gdn\"], \"expected_impact\": \"Explains how a prior round's patch could be approved and integrated yet change nothing, and redirects future vllm-side authoring to the live tree or to a proposal.\", \"source\": \"/usr/local/bin/vllm-wu1w; diff -rq --exclude=__pycache__ of the two vllm trees; state.json enablement.framework_root; manifest.json dependencies.magpie.path\", \"what\": \"ROUTING FACT for any future patch authoring here: the serving interpreter is NOT the allowlisted /opt/envs/vllm tree. VLLM_BIN=/usr/local/bin/vllm-wu1w execs /opt/envs/wu1w/bin/python -m vllm.entrypoints.cli.main, so a vllm-side patch authored against /opt/envs/vllm/.../vllm is INERT on the gate. The two trees are near-identical 0.28.0 builds differing in exactly 3 source files (_aiter_ops.py, _custom_ops.py, model\n## residual_questions:\n - EVAL-PATH RISK for the accuracy gate (I deliberately did NOT touch it - altering it would be changing the eval contract): this checkpoint's chat_template.jinja injects a large built-in operator system prompt plus xhigh reasoning-effort instructions. Measured live: a 12-token one-line user question cost prompt_tokens=1225, and the model emits a long <|im_start|> reasoning block before its answer (the chat probe reasoned out loud, then printed '42'). If the gate's gsm8k eval goes through /v1/chat/completions, that ~1.2k-token prefix plus CoT tail can press against max_model_len=6144 and can defe\n - Should the next round keep BOTH the approved Magpie reconciliation patch and this env pin? They are mutually consistent (both resolve to HIP=0), so either alone boots and both together are harmless - but if re-application of 001_reconcile_rocm_device_masks.patch ever fails, this proposal is the patch-free safety net that still boots. I authored no replacement patch to avoid duplicating already-approved work.\n - Port hygiene between attempts: attempt[1] died on 'OSError: [Errno 98] Address already in use' on gate port 8888 because a server from failed attempt[0] still held it. Is there a pre-flight port release before a retry? I did not kill any foreign pid (Iron Rule 7), so this can recur on a retry-after-failure and would again be misclassified as a model-side launch failure.\n## proposals:\n - rocm_logical_hip_mask_pin | Makes the combo boot. The harness inherits HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=2 (a PHYSICAL id) while the gate config pins ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0; ROCR filters at the HSA layer and re-indexes survivors to 0..n-1, so HIP must carry the LOGICAL index. Because the counts are equal, torch's length check passes and the | args:  | envs: {'CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES': '0', 'HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES': '0'}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0475c2f4-1a0e-481c-86a6-d19f3a20bb66","uuid":"97c7a35b-b0a6-4d54-a5e1-97a4d7ac339f","timestamp":"2026-09-14T16:08:53.972Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## summary : Gap is a ROCm device-mask leak, not a model gap: Qwen3_5ForConditionalGeneration IS registered and runnable in the live serving env (/opt/envs/wu1w). A/B on the real Magpie path under the inherited leak (ROCR=0 vs HIP=2): control -> EngineCore 'No CUDA GPUs are available'; with only the proposed extra_envs HIP/CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 (logical index) -> SUCCESS, /health 200, result.json. No new patch: the kept reconciliation patch applies cleanly; the client install is verified live.\n## confidence : 0.9\n## empty : False\n## gap_canonical_id : gap.enablement.unknown\n## domain : enablement_specialist\n## patches_written: []\n## artifacts: []\n## setup_commands: []\n## new_findings:\n - {\"accuracy_risk\": \"none\", \"domain_tags\": [\"vllm\", \"qwen3_5\", \"gdn\", \"hybrid_attention\", \"runnability\", \"enablement\", \"gfx90a\"], \"expected_impact\": \"Reframes the round entirely: no ladder climb (Rung 2-5) is needed for this model, so a config-only delta is the correct and sufficient deliverable.\", \"source\": \"/mnt/stripe-3mix-3t2/models/davetha/Qwen3.8-27B-ABLITERATED-W8A8-gdnint8/config.json; /opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/model_executor/models/registry.py:203-204,592-595; in-session logs/repro_server.log + logs/reproB_fixed.log (port 8899, GPU 0, exact production server_args from manifest.json)\", \"what\": \"The gap 'vllm cannot launch Qwen3.8-27B-ABLITERATED-W8A8-gdnint8: unknown' is NOT an architecture/weight/kernel enablement gap. architectures=['Qwen3_5For