ure_kind=unknown). Authored a 158-line pure-insertion patch to Magpie's _build_local_command that reconciles HIP/CUDA to the LOGICAL 0..n-1 set ROCR re-indexes to (the rule the InferenceX launcher already states but cannot apply to an inherited value), with vendor guard + fail-open so it is inert on CUDA and on already-valid masks. PROVEN END-TO-END: ran the real Magpie serving path under a deliberately leaked parent env with the patch on PYTHONPATH -> logs 'Device-mask reconciliation for local run: HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES: 2 -> 0', weights load, 35/35 CUDA graphs capture, GET /health 200 OK. Cleared the reported launch gap. NEXT DEEPER FAILURE now exposed: the bench CLIENT interpreter /opt/venv/bin/python3 lacks huggingface_hub+transformers (benchmark_lib.sh:682 bare 'python3'), so no inferencex_result.json is produced - a chicken-and-egg gap because the harness installs them only in run_eval, after the client has already died. Also established why attempt 2's patch was likely REVERTED: it targeted /opt/envs/vllm/.../vllm, but the server runs from /opt/envs/wu1w via VLLM_BIN, so such a patch is inert; and an env fix pinning HIP to a same-length physical id passes torch's length check yet yields is_available()==False.\",\n/home/qiba/ROCm.AI/hyperloom/session/Qwen3.8-27B-ABLITERATED-W8A8-gdnint8/20260914T134902Z-244d9455/reports/enablement/patches/001_001_reconcile_rocm_device_masks.patch:181:+            logger.warning(\"Device-mask reconciliation for local run: %s\", repair)\n/home/qiba/ROCm.AI/hyperloom/session/Qwen3.8-27B-ABLITERATED-W8A8-gdnint8/20260914T134902Z-244d9455/reports/enablement/b8dc969b654d45e2a1e07acf784a2a4e/patches/001_reconcile_rocm_device_masks.patch:181:+            logger.warning(\"Device-mask reconciliation for local run: %s\", repair)\n/home/qiba/ROCm.AI/hyperloom/session/Qwen3.8-27B-ABLITERATED-W8A8-gdnint8/20260914T134902Z-244d9455/reports/enablement/30ccc757c22d476390bae0873bfa153b/patches/001_reconcile_rocm_device_masks.patch:181:+          