e_masks /opt/envs/vllm/.../Magpie/modes/benchmark/\"\n \"benchmarker.py == 0 right now — the tree is unpatched again.\")\nf[1][\"source\"]=(\"hyperloom/common/visible_devices.py:52-96; hyperloom/common/env_safety.py:286-357 \"\n \"(is_allowed_variant_env_key / BLOCKED_* sets, probed live in-session); \"\n \"executors/_workload_envs.py:1054-1097; executors/baseline.py:3519-3532; executors/_grid_runner.py:664-671; \"\n \"runs/baseline/48e0ae2b0af74c03b4b40c847fc99d3b/baseline_config.with_envs.yaml and \"\n \"runs/baseline/0668d71b42d54c559c36634e823a55a5/baseline_config.with_envs.yaml; runs/integrate_patch/*/patch_backups/\")\nf[1][\"expected_impact\"]=(\"Stops the next round from re-proposing an env pin as the baseline remedy (it is only honoured on the variant \"\n \"path) and identifies the one shared layer that can fix it durably.\")\nd[\"payload\"][\"residual_questions\"][0]=(\"Patch 002 is the mechanism; please do not rely on the accepted env pin alone. Measured: is_allowed_variant_env_key(\"\n \"'HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES')==True, so a pin survives materialisation IF handed — but baseline.py:3519 only reads \"\n \"params['extra_envs'], and both failing baselines (48e0ae2b 15:14, 0668d71b 15:51) rendered ROCR='0' with no HIP/CUDA \"\n \"key, i.e. the accumulated accepted_config never reached the baseline launch, only the grid/variant path \"\n \"(_grid_runner.py:670). That asymmetry is why the prior round's rebench passed while the gate kept failing. With 002 \"\n \"integrated the pin is redundant (002 writes the same logical mask on every path); if 002 is rejected, the pin alone \"\n \"will not rescue the baseline.\")\nt=os.path.join(D,\"specialist_done.json.tmp\"); open(t,'w').write(json.dumps(d,indent=2)); os.replace(t,os.path.join(D,\"specialist_done.json\"))\nprint(\"FINAL written; findings:\",len(f),\"proposals:\",len(d[\"payload\"][\"proposal_set\"]),\"patches:\",d[\"payload\"][\"patches_written\"])\nprint(\"bytes:\",os.path.getsize(os.path.join(D,\"specialist_